  "question": {
    "text": "The area of the region bounded by the curves $x\\left(1+y^2\\right)=1$ and $y^2=2 x$ is:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "gDbds",
      "text": "$2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}-\\frac{1}{3}\\right)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "KkAdg",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{2}-\\frac{1}{3}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "tZg2q",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{4}-\\frac{1}{3}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "tnCQv",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}-\\frac{1}{3}\\right)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned}\n& x\\left(1+y^2\\right)=1 \\\\\n& y^2=2 x\n\\end{aligned}$\n\nFrom equation (1) \\& (2)\n$\\begin{aligned}\nx(1+2 x)=1 & \\Rightarrow 2 x^2+x-1=0 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow x=\\frac{1}{2}, x=-1 \\text { (Reject) } \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow y^2=2\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow y= \\pm 1\n\\end{aligned}$\n\n\n\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/6X7_oonfV008fb8YzDu68cVXBrvdK8nbqoFps5zZCMg.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n\n\n\n$\\begin{aligned} \\text { Area bounded } & =\\int_{-1}^1\\left(\\frac{1}{1+y^2}-\\frac{y^2}{2}\\right) d y \\\\ & =\\left.\\left(\\tan ^{-1} y-\\frac{y^3}{6}\\right)\\right|_{-1} ^1 \\\\ & =\\frac{\\pi}{2}-\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
